Elif shows me the large espresso machine.
It shines and looks very professional.
"We got this machine as a donation," Elif explains.
"You have to learn to be patient with it," she says.
She has already ground coffee beans.
Then she shows me the first important step.
"We have to press the coffee powder down completely straight," she explains.
Elif does that and starts the machine.
The coffee flows slowly into the small cup.
It looks perfect and smells wonderful.
I watch closely, because I have to learn to operate the machine properly.
The neighbourhood café is still very quiet.
So we have enough time to practice.
"Now it is your turn," Elif says and gives me the portafilter.
I fill fresh coffee powder into the portafilter.
Then I try to press the powder down firmly.
"A little firmer still," Elif corrects me kindly.
My second attempt is already much better.
We practice together for a few more minutes.
Then I am ready for my first guest.
